# CODEOWNERS — review ownership by area.
#
# Referenced by docs/governance/SECURITY.md ("reports about deployment go to
# CODEOWNERS for deployment/") and GOVERNANCE.md §1/§3 (a limit or contract
# change needs the owning reviewer). GitHub requires a review from every
# matching owner before a PR to a protected branch can merge; the last
# matching pattern wins.
#
# Single-owner repository: every path is owned by @AshJha0, because the
# organisation teams (@iap/platform, @iap/risk, ...) this file used to name
# never existed and GitHub reported them as CODEOWNERS errors. The per-area
# split below is kept so that, when more maintainers exist, only the handles
# need to change. Areas: platform/deployment/observability/CI, risk engine and
# limits, core (market data, book, codecs, replay), execution (simulator, SOR,
# algos, TCA), research (features, alphas, models, papers), docs/contracts.
# Note: GitHub does not let a PR author approve their own PR, so a rule that
# requires code-owner review needs a second maintainer (REPO_SETTINGS.md).

